## 2026-08-07 — bounded-context-map.md (missing map view)

**Artifact:** `sandbox/courier/.context/bounded-context-map.md`
**Rule:** `ddd.md` bounded_context — "Draw context boundaries, dependency arcs"; produce an inventory + diagram + arc summary, THEN building blocks detail under each context

**Wrong:** Document dives straight into per-context building blocks (aggregates, stereotypes, invariants) without a strategic map view at the top. A bounded context map must first show the MAP: context inventory, a visual representation of boundaries and arcs, and integration arc summaries. What we generated is entirely tactical DDD (building blocks) with no map.

**Correct:** Structure is: (1) `## Context Map` — ASCII diagram + context inventory + arc summaries; THEN (2) per-context building blocks sections (`## Routing`, `## PackageIntake`, `## Fleet`) with aggregate + stereotype detail; THEN (3) `## Dependencies` with full arc detail. The "map" part is the first section — without it the document is just a building blocks registry, not a context map.

**When:** spec / generate / gen-ddd pass — generated building_blocks fidelity detail without adding the strategic map view first


**Artifact:** `sandbox/courier/.context/bounded-context-map.md`
**Rule:** `ddd.md` — building_blocks deepens the same context map, calls clean_engineering; CE is the downstream artifact; do not restate class contracts in two places

**Wrong:** Generated bounded-context-map.md with full CE-format class contracts (all properties, all operations, Invariant lines per operation) AND ALSO generated clean-engineering-model.md with the same contracts. Two unlinked models carrying the same class structure — bounded-context-map used CE `+` prefix, `<<composition>>` / `<<association>>` property markers, and typed operation signatures, duplicating everything already in CE.

**Correct:** DDD bounded-context-map owns the domain semantic layer: context boundaries, owning teams, aggregate root identification, DDD stereotypes (`<<Aggregate Root>>`, `<<Value Object>>`, etc.), key domain invariants (aggregate-level, not per-operation), and cross-context integration wiring. CE owns the full class contracts (I{Type} model + concrete {Type} spec with relationship markers, interactions, full invariants). DDD class blocks should carry DDD stereotype + the top-level domain invariants + reference to CE for full contracts — not re-state every property and operation.

**When:** spec / generate / gen-ddd pass — DDD generated full CE-style class contracts without checking whether CE model existed or would be generated alongside


**Artifact:** `sandbox/courier/.context/story-map.md`, `story-context.md`, `thin-slice.md`
**Rule:** `stories` — at spec fidelity every story must be explicitly named; `* approx X more stories` is discovery/scaffold language

**Wrong:** story-map.md retained 8 `* approx X more stories (hint)` placeholder lines inside a spec-fidelity artifact. story-context.md listed only 15 of ~22 stories. thin-slice.md placed only 4 stories (Increment 1) leaving 18 stories unplaced.

**Correct:** Once past scaffold/discovery, every story must be named explicitly — no approximation lines. All stories must be placed into an increment in thin-slice. The `* approx` form is only acceptable at discovery fidelity where the full mechanics haven't been grilled.

**When:** spec / generate / gen-stories pass — story-map.md written with approx lines carried over from sketch scaffold

